  "description": "Under the fixture policy, withdrawing the directive itself, its expectation's only support, ends the expectation property at the same instant. The directive was withdrawn at the last of the endings it waited for, so the policy ends the first period with cause withdrawal, citing the withdrawal; and the baseline begins a second period at that instant, cause review_withdrawn. One write records, in order, the first period's policy end act, the second period's begin act and the property's end act. The story is open, unreviewed and pending again, with no open child.",
  "note": "7.6.7: \"An expectation property whose first period is nested under exactly one story (7.6.15), because a review of that story began it, is part of that story, its middle: its begin and end acts, and the revisions of them (7.6.10), are Assertions on that story Item in the same form, `(story, <event context>, story)`.\" The act names follow README section 7, Story-held expectation property acts: `(<story>, \"<story>/exp:<path>/b<n>\", <story>)`, with `/e<n>` and `/v<n>` likewise.",
